# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots xinetd with the rsh + rlogin stanzas enabled and then
# execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the r-services are ALREADY LISTENING on 514/513 when the agent starts,
#     which is what makes "removed /etc/xinetd.d/rsh but never stopped xinetd"
#     detectable - a running xinetd keeps serving the stanzas it loaded at
#     startup;
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so stopping xinetd cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: the live listener must be STOPPED, not just
# disabled on disk.
